# language: en

Feature: UnSubscribe

    Scenario Outline: The unsubscribe request for a signal that is currently subscribed has been successfully processed
        Given a signal at <path> is set to <value_0> of datatype <datatype>
        And attempts to subscribe the signal at <path> of datatype <datatype> is succeeded
        Then attempts to unsubscribe the signal at <path> of datatype <datatype> is succeeded

    Examples:
        | path                                                     | datatype  | value_0     |
        | Vehicle.Cabin.Convertible.IsOpen | bool | false |
        | Vehicle.Cabin.Convertible.Position | uint8 | 50 |
        | Vehicle.Cabin.HVAC.AmbientAirTemperature | float | 0.0 |
        | Vehicle.Cabin.HVAC.Station.Row1.DriverSide.AirDistribution | string | MIDDLE |
        | Vehicle.Cabin.Seat.Row1.DriverSide.Backrest.HeatingCooling | int8 | 0 |
        | Vehicle.Cabin.Seat.Row1.DriverSide.Height | uint16 | 32767 |
        


    Scenario Outline: Unsubscribe of one subscription_id does not hinder other subscription_ids
        Given a signal at <path> is set to <value_0> of datatype <datatype>
        And attempts to subscribe the signal at <path> of datatype <datatype> for <count> times with duplex <duplex> are all succeeded
        When attempts to unsubscribe the signal at <path> of datatype <datatype> is succeeded
        And the value of signal at <path> changes to <value_1> of datatype <datatype>
        Then The other subscription_ids stream returns <datatype> <value_1> on <path>

    Examples:
        | path                                                     | count         | duplex        | datatype      | value_0       | value_1       |
        | Vehicle.Cabin.Convertible.IsOpen | 2 | 1 | bool | false | true |
        | Vehicle.Cabin.Convertible.Position | 2 | 1 | uint8 | 50 | 100 |
        | Vehicle.Cabin.HVAC.AmbientAirTemperature | 2 | 1 | float | 0.0 | 3.4028235e+38 |
        | Vehicle.Cabin.HVAC.Station.Row1.DriverSide.AirDistribution | 2 | 1 | string | MIDDLE | UP |
        | Vehicle.Cabin.Seat.Row1.DriverSide.Backrest.HeatingCooling | 2 | 1 | int8 | 0 | 100 |
        | Vehicle.Cabin.Seat.Row1.DriverSide.Height | 2 | 1 | uint16 | 32767 | 65535 |
        


    Scenario Outline: Millions of unsubscribe requests do not kill kura server
        Given a signal at <path> is set to <value_0> of datatype <datatype>
        When attempts to subscribe the signal at <path> of datatype <datatype> for <count> times with duplex <duplex> are all succeeded
        Then HeadlessApp unsubscribe the sensor signal <path> of <datatype> to close connections with duplex <duplex> are all succeeded

    Examples:
        | path                                                     | count            | duplex           | datatype      | value_0       | value_1       |
        | Vehicle.Cabin.Convertible.IsOpen | 100 | 10 | bool | false | true |
        | Vehicle.Cabin.Convertible.Position | 100 | 10 | uint8 | 50 | 100 |
        | Vehicle.Cabin.HVAC.AmbientAirTemperature | 100 | 10 | float | 0.0 | 3.4028235e+38 |
        | Vehicle.Cabin.HVAC.Station.Row1.DriverSide.AirDistribution | 100 | 10 | string | MIDDLE | UP |
        | Vehicle.Cabin.Seat.Row1.DriverSide.Backrest.HeatingCooling | 100 | 10 | int8 | 0 | 100 |
        | Vehicle.Cabin.Seat.Row1.DriverSide.Height | 100 | 10 | uint16 | 32767 | 65535 |
        


    @CleanupRestoreNetwork
    Scenario Outline: Unsubscribe requests during network failure result in client error
        Given HeadlessApp subscribe the sensor signal <path> which is initialized <value> of datatype <datatype>
        When network failure of <network_failure> is injected
        Then attempts to unsubscribe the subscription to <path> of <datatype> are failed

    Examples:
        | path                                          | network_failure | datatype  | value     |
        | Vehicle.Cabin.Convertible.IsOpen | reject  | bool | false |
        | Vehicle.Cabin.Convertible.IsOpen | timeout | bool | false |
        | Vehicle.Cabin.Convertible.Position | reject  | uint8 | 50 |
        | Vehicle.Cabin.Convertible.Position | timeout | uint8 | 50 |
        | Vehicle.Cabin.HVAC.AmbientAirTemperature | reject  | float | 0.0 |
        | Vehicle.Cabin.HVAC.AmbientAirTemperature | timeout | float | 0.0 |
        | Vehicle.Cabin.HVAC.Station.Row1.DriverSide.AirDistribution | reject  | string | MIDDLE |
        | Vehicle.Cabin.HVAC.Station.Row1.DriverSide.AirDistribution | timeout | string | MIDDLE |
        | Vehicle.Cabin.Seat.Row1.DriverSide.Backrest.HeatingCooling | reject  | int8 | 0 |
        | Vehicle.Cabin.Seat.Row1.DriverSide.Backrest.HeatingCooling | timeout | int8 | 0 |
        | Vehicle.Cabin.Seat.Row1.DriverSide.Height | reject  | uint16 | 32767 |
        | Vehicle.Cabin.Seat.Row1.DriverSide.Height | timeout | uint16 | 32767 |
        


    Scenario Outline: Unsubscribe requests after recovery from network failure are succeeded
        Given HeadlessApp subscribe the sensor signal <path> which is initialized <value> of datatype <datatype>
